error[NK1201]: You can't put the struct `lib::Node` in an `f"…"` hole.
  --> src/main.nika:5:3
   |
 5 | 		println(f"{n}")
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A hole is written as its value's text, and a struct that is not an error has no text form. `n` is `lib::Node`.
   = help: Write its fields in holes of their own: `{n.line}`, `{n.raw}`.
error[NK1201]: You can't print the `enum` `lib::Kind`.
  --> src/main.nika:7:2
   |
 7 | 	println(lib::Kind::Plain)
   |  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A print call writes its value's text, and an `enum` that is not an error has no text form. `lib::Kind::Plain` is `lib::Kind`.
   = help: Match on it and give each variant its text first, or print `f"{(lib::Kind::Plain):?}"` for its debug form.
